<title>PORTUGAL: BCP, BPI hit 1997 highs.</title>
<headline>BCP, BPI hit 1997 highs.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Portuguese banks Banco Comercial Portugues and Banco Portugues de Investimento hit highs for 1997 amid optimism over their results, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors are back in the banking sector, propelling BCP and BPI to new highs, but there is little volume and a degree of speculation,&quot; said one dealer who asked not to be identified.</p>
<p>BCP hit a high of 3,348 escudos and BPI 2,940.</p>
<p>Dealers said recent buy recommendations for banks by Portuguese investment houses and the recent promotion of Portugal to the status of developed market by Morgan Stanley had raised interest in banking stocks by foreign investors.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
